solnix: the solnix: flake input scheme

  nix shell solnix:#hello                 the supported edition (the repo's default branch)
  nix shell solnix:unstable#hello         a branch
  nix shell solnix:v2026.08.07#hello      a tag
  nix shell solnix:f368c25#hello          a commit id, full or abbreviated (>= 7 hex digits)
  nix shell solnix:solnix-pkgs/main#x     another repository on the same host

Each form is rewritten to an ordinary git input (git+https://git.solnix.io/<repo>.git, or $NIX_SOLNIX_GIT_URL),
so lock files, caching and `nix flake metadata` are those of git+https, and a lock written on solnix reads back on
any Nix. The scheme does only what a registry entry cannot: a tag (Nix 2.24 fetches a bare ref as refs/heads/) and
an abbreviated commit id (the git fetcher needs 40 hex digits). Both are resolved once at parse time against the
remote with git ls-remote, or a fetch of the branches plus rev-parse for an id below a branch tip.

fetchers.cc: Input::fromURL no longer overwrites the scheme of an input whose inputFromURL already bound one, so
the rewritten input keeps the git scheme.

solnix: is the explicit, OS-independent spelling. On a solnix system `nixpkgs#hello` also means solnix's package
set, through the system flake registry (modules/config/nix-channel.nix), the way NixOS points `nixpkgs` at its own.

